.policy "ruff-n813-camelcase-imported-as-lowercase" revision 2
.description "Keep the alias of an imported CamelCase name in CamelCase; a lowercase alias makes readers mistake a class for a function or variable."
.language python
.mode steer
.scope include "**/*"

// Ruff N813 (pep8-naming): a CamelCase name imported under an all-lowercase alias. Exempt when the name or the
// alias matches `pep8-naming.ignore-names`.
//   from mod import CamelCase as camelcase    ← N813
#include "python/naming.rr"

.violation N813(at: node, x: symbol, a: symbol) code "N813"
    "Use a CamelCase alias instead of `{a}` for `{x}` and update its uses; leave it if `{x}` is really a function or variable despite its CamelCase name."
    suppress ruff "N813"
N813(i, x, a) :- alias_import(i, x, a), camel_name(x), cased_lower(a), !naming_ignored(x), !naming_ignored(a).
